@@host: Eighteen-oh-six. The painter Philipp Otto Runge sends a publisher in Heidelberg a story from the Baltic coast of Pomerania, written down in the fishermen's own dialect.

@@host: Six years later the Brothers Grimm print it, dialect and all, in their first collection of tales. Every time the fisherman walks down to the shore, listen to the sea.

