@wife: The next morning when Dame Ilsabill awoke it was broad daylight, and she jogged the fisherman with her elbow, and said, “Get up, husband, and bestir yourself, for we must be king of all the land.”

@fisherman,wife: “Wife, wife,” said the man, “why should we wish to be the king? I will not be king.” “Then I will,” said she.

@fisherman,wife: “But, wife,” said the fisherman, “how can you be king? The fish cannot make you a king.” “Husband,” said she, “say no more about it, but go and try! I will be king.”

